    &lt;h2&gt;
      Exercises to accompany Predicate Tutorial 5&lt;/h2&gt;
    &lt;h3&gt;
      Exercise 1 (of 1).
    &lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;
      The propositional rules of inference are used unchanged in predicate 
      logic.
    &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;
      Derive
    &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;
      
    &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;blockquote&gt;
      a) Fa ∴ ∼ ∼ Fa
    &lt;/blockquote&gt;
    &lt;blockquote&gt;
      b) ∴ ∼ (Fb&amp;amp; ∼ Fb)
    &lt;/blockquote&gt;
    &lt;blockquote&gt;
      c) ∼ Fm&amp;amp; ∼ Gn∴ ∼ (Fm∨Gn)
    &lt;/blockquote&gt;
    &lt;blockquote&gt;
      d) (Fa&amp;amp;Fa)∨(Gb&amp;amp;Gb)∴ Fa∨Gb
    &lt;/blockquote&gt;
    &lt;blockquote&gt;
      e) Fb⊃(Ga⊃Hc), Fb⊃Ga ∴ Fb⊃Hc
    &lt;/blockquote&gt;
    &lt;blockquote&gt;
      f) Fa∨Gb, Gb⊃Hd ∴ ( ∼ Fa⊃Hd)
    &lt;/blockquote&gt;
    &lt;blockquote&gt;
      g) (Fa⊃Gb)&amp;amp;(Gb⊃Fa) ∴ Fa≡Gb
    &lt;/blockquote&gt;
  

